---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const effectiveDate = 'June 19, 2026';
const description =
  'Terms of Use for Simple Fasting, including health disclaimers, acceptable use, local data responsibility, and service limitations.';
---

<Layout title="Terms of Use — Simple Fasting" description={description} legal>
  <header class="legal-hero">
    <div class="shell">
      <p class="legal-meta">Effective {effectiveDate}</p>
      <h1>Terms of Use</h1>
      <p>
        These terms govern your use of the Simple Fasting mobile application and website. Please
        read the health and data-responsibility sections carefully.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <div class="legal-content shell">
    <nav class="legal-toc" aria-label="Terms sections">
      <a href="#acceptance">Acceptance</a>
      <a href="#health">Health disclaimer</a>
      <a href="#license">App license</a>
      <a href="#use">Acceptable use</a>
      <a href="#data">Your data</a>
      <a href="#services">Availability</a>
      <a href="#warranty">Disclaimers</a>
      <a href="#liability">Liability</a>
      <a href="#changes">Changes</a>
      <a href="#contact">Contact</a>
    </nav>

    <article class="prose">
      <section id="acceptance">
        <h2>1. Acceptance</h2>
        <p>
          By downloading, accessing, or using Simple Fasting, you agree to these Terms of Use and
          the <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>. If you do not agree, do not use the app or
          website.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="health">
        <h2>2. Health and medical disclaimer</h2>
        <p>
          Simple Fasting is a tracking tool. It does not provide medical advice, diagnosis,
          treatment, nutrition advice, or emergency services. Timers, reminders, statistics, and
          goals are informational only and do not determine whether fasting is safe for you.
        </p>
        <p>
          Consult a qualified healthcare professional before fasting, especially if you are
          pregnant or breastfeeding, under 18, have diabetes or another medical condition, take
          medication, have a history of an eating disorder, or experience symptoms while fasting.
          Stop fasting and seek appropriate care if you feel unwell. Do not delay professional care
          because of information shown by the app.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="license">
        <h2>3. Permission to use the app</h2>
        <p>
          Subject to these terms and applicable store rules, you receive a limited, personal,
          non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable permission to install and use Simple Fasting
          for lawful personal purposes. No ownership rights are transferred to you.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="use">
        <h2>4. Acceptable use</h2>
        <p>You agree not to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Use the app or website unlawfully or to harm another person.</li>
          <li>Misrepresent the app as medical advice or a substitute for professional care.</li>
          <li>Interfere with, damage, or attempt unauthorized access to the app or website.</li>
          <li>Remove ownership notices or distribute modified copies in violation of applicable law.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="data">
        <h2>5. Local data and backups</h2>
        <p>
          The current app stores fasting history and preferences locally. You are responsible for
          maintaining access to your device, creating exports you wish to keep, and selecting safe
          export destinations. Clearing data, uninstalling the app, device loss, storage failure,
          or operating-system behavior may result in data loss. We cannot recover data that was
          never transmitted to us.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="services">
        <h2>6. Stores, devices, and third-party services</h2>
        <p>
          App stores, device operating systems, email providers, export destinations, and links to
          third-party sites are operated by others. Their terms and privacy policies apply to their
          services. Features may vary by device, operating-system version, permission settings, and
          platform availability.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="warranty">
        <h2>7. Availability and warranty disclaimer</h2>
        <p>
          The app and website are provided on an “as available” basis. To the extent permitted by
          law, we do not promise uninterrupted operation, perfect accuracy, compatibility with every
          device, or preservation of local data. Mandatory warranties and consumer rights that
          cannot legally be excluded remain unaffected.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="liability">
        <h2>8. Limitation of liability</h2>
        <p>
          To the extent permitted by applicable law, Simple Fasting and its contributors are not
          liable for indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive losses arising from
          use of the app or website, including health decisions, missed notifications, or local data
          loss. This limitation does not apply where liability cannot legally be limited.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="changes">
        <h2>9. Changes and termination</h2>
        <p>
          We may update the app, website, or these terms. Revised terms will be posted with a new
          effective date. You may stop using the service at any time. We may restrict access when
          reasonably necessary to address unlawful use, security, or discontinued operation.
        </p>
        <p>
          These terms are governed by applicable law. Mandatory consumer protections and rights in
          your place of residence remain in effect.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="contact">
        <h2>10. Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about these terms can be sent to
          <a href="mailto:support@simplefasting.app">support@simplefasting.app</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </article>
  </div>
</Layout>
